[Term]
id: UBERON:0000048
name: pinhole eye
def: "Simple eye that has a small aperture (which may be adjustable) and deep pit. It is only found in the nautiloids." [DOI:10.1146/annurev.ne.15.030192.000245, Wikipedia:Pinhole_eye]
subset: grouping_class
