[Term]
id: UBERON:0000121
name: perineurium
def: "A layer of thin, concentrically arranged cells with interspersed collagen that lies within the epineurium. The perineurium is a component of the blood–nerve barrier and is essential for protecting axons and their associated Schwann cells from ionic flux, toxins and infection." [NLXANAT:090205, PMID:18434767, PMID:25818566]
