property_value: external_definition "The renal veins are veins that drain the kidney. They connect the kidney to the inferior vena cava. It is usually singular to each kidney, except in the condition 'multiple renal veins'. It also divides into 2 divisions upon entering the kidney: the anterior branch which receives blood from the anterior portion of the kidney and, the posterior branch which receives blood from the posterior portion. Often, each renal vein will have a branch that receives blood from the ureter. [WP,unvetted][Wikipedia:Renal_vein]." xsd:string {source="Wikipedia:Renal_vein"}
property_value: external_ontology_notes "in EHDAA2, the renal vein is part of the kidney" xsd:string {external_ontology="EHDAA2"}

