property_value: depiction "http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/29/Illu_pelvic_girdle.jpg" xsd:anyURI
property_value: external_definition "Cavity for the articulation of the proximal bone of the hind limb.[AAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-06-20", external_class="AAO:0000770", ontology="AAO", source="AAO:LAP"}
property_value: external_ontology_notes "whilst WP defines this as a surface, MA treats it as a bone. There are other FMA classes that may be better suited to representing the surface." xsd:string {external_ontology="MA"}
property_value: homology_notes "During the transformation from the osteolepiform fins to tetrapod limbs, the appendages and girdles underwent a number of radical changes. The pelvic girdle became a weight-bearing structure by evolution of an ischium, a full mesio-ventral contact between the two sides of the girdle, an ilium, and a contact between the vertebral column and the girdle through a sacral rib. Fore- and hindlimbs shifted laterally by reorientation of the glenoid and the acetabulum.[well established][VHOG]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-09-17", external_class="VHOG:0000974", ontology="VHOG", source="DOI:10.1038/nature04119 Boisvert CA, The pelvic fin and girdle of Panderichthys and the origin of tetrapod locomotion. Nature (2005)", source="http://bgee.unil.ch/"}
property_value: taxon_notes "In reptiles and in birds, the acetabula are deep sockets." xsd:string {source="WP"}

