def: "The organism subdivision that includes the pelvic girdle skeleton and associated soft tissue. Note that this includes both the skeletal elements and associated tissues (integument, muscle, etc). Examples: There are only two instances in an organism, right and left pelvic girdle regions." [DOI:10.1002/dvdy.22617, FMA:16581, FMA:23217, https://groups.google.com/d/topic/obo-anatomy/h4R4xKmINrw/discussion, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165, UBERONREF:0000003]
