[Term]
id: UBERON:0001286
name: Bowman's space
def: "A narrow chalice-shaped cavity between the glomerular and capsular epithelium of the glomerular capsule of the kidney[TFD]. Between the visceral and parietal layers, into which the filtrate enters after passing through the podocytes' filtration slits[WP]. luminal region between the glomerular capsule visceral and parietal layers, into which filtrate enters after passing through the filtration barrier from the glomerular capillaries[MP]." [http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/bowman's+space, MP:0011499, Wikipedia:Bowman's_space]
