[Term]
id: UBERON:0001320
name: iliolumbar vein
def: "The iliolumbar vein is the vena comitans of the iliolumbar artery. The obturator nerve crosses superficial to it. A single vein is found more commonly than a double vein. It drains vertebral segments four and five. It is closely related to the ascending lumbar vein. [WP,unvetted]." [Wikipedia:Iliolumbar_vein]
