property_value: editor_note "TODO - check AAO placement; in rodents this is fused with the lunate to make the scapholunate" xsd:string
property_value: external_definition "One of two element that constitute the basal row of carpals. It articulates proximally with the radius, mesially with the ulnare (or pars intermedia of the ulnare when the ulnare is fused to the intermedium) and distally with the centrale (also recognized by some authors as element Y). This element originates from one or two condensation centers. Occasionally it may fuse to carpal 5(4), the ulnare, or other elements.[AAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-06-20", external_class="AAO:0000790", ontology="AAO", source="AAO:LAP"}
property_value: external_definition "the bone of the hand located at the radial side of the carpus and which articulates with the radius, trapezium, trapezoideum, capitate, and lunate bones" xsd:string {source="MP:0010775,MGI:llw2"}
property_value: terminology_notes "In reptiles, birds, and amphibians, this bone is instead commonly referred to as the radiale, because of its articulation with the radius[WP]" xsd:string

