property_value: external_comment "Dermopalatine: same as palatine. The prefix is used by fish people because the palatine is a dermal replacement bone for a section of the autopalatine section of the palatoquadrate. In that context, palatine is potentially ambiguous.[Palaeos]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-09-17", source="http://palaeos.com/vertebrates/glossary/glossaryD.html"}
property_value: external_comment "In ostariophysans, the dermopalatine is absent.[TAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-09-06", external_class="TAO:0000015", ontology="TAO", source="Curator"}
property_value: external_definition "Dermal bone that forms the antero-lateral region of the palate and is located ventral to the autopalatine. The dermopalatine is bilaterally paired and usually bears teeth.[TAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-08-14", external_class="TAO:0000015", ontology="TAO", source="TAO:GA_TG"}
