property_value: external_definition "Paired, intramembranous bones that lie at the posterolateral margins of the skull. Lateral and dorsal to the quadrate.[AAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-06-20", external_class="AAO:0000574", ontology="AAO", source="AAO:EJS"}
property_value: external_definition "The squamosal bone is part of the dermatocranium in early tetrapods and becomes part of the mammalian occipital and temporal bones. [Bemis_WE, Functional_Anatomy_of_the_Vertebrates:_An_Evolutionary_Perspective, Grande_L, Third_Edition_(2001)_Orlando_Fla.:_Harcourt_College_Publishers, Walker_WF, p.246, see_Liem_KF][VHOG]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-09-17", external_class="VHOG:0001561", ontology="VHOG", source="http://bgee.unil.ch/"}
property_value: taxon_notes "The squamosal bone, which is homologous with the squama, and forms the side of the cranium in many bony fish and tetrapods. Primitively, it is a flattened plate-like bone, but in many animals it is narrower in form, for example, where it forms the boundary between the two temporal fenestrae of diapsid reptiles" xsd:string

