[Term]
id: UBERON:0001991
name: cervical ganglion
def: "The cervical ganglia are paravertebral ganglia of the sympathetic nervous system. They consist of three paravertebral ganglia: superior cervical ganglion middle cervical ganglion inferior cervical ganglion. The inferior ganglion may be fused with the first thoracic ganglion to form a single structure, the stellate ganglion. Nerves emerging from cervical sympathetic ganglia contribute to the cardiac plexus, among other things. [WP,unvetted]." [Wikipedia:Cervical_ganglion]
subset: uberon_slim
synonym: "cervical sympathetic ganglion" EXACT []
