[Term]
id: UBERON:0002984
name: lateral dorsal nucleus
def: "The lateral dorsal nucleus is a nucleus of the thalamus. It acts in concert with the anterior nuclei of thalamus. It receives significant input from several subdivisions of visual cortex, and has a primary output to parietal cortex on the dorsolateral cortical convexity, giving it access to limbic forebrain nuclei important for emotion and behavior functions." [Wikipedia:Lateral_dorsal_nucleus_of_thalamus]
