property_value: axiom_lost_from_external_ontology "relationship loss: part_of caudal fin skeleton (VSAO:0000167)[TAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-08-14", external_class="TAO:0000158", ontology="TAO"}
property_value: external_comment "In zebrafish, it is composed of preural vertebra 1 and ural centra 1 and 2. The number of ural centra that become fused with preural centrum 1 varies among teleost subgroups. Because of varying developmental origins the urostyle may not be homologous across species.[TAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-09-06", external_class="TAO:0000158", ontology="TAO", source="Curator"}
property_value: external_definition "Anatomical cluster that is the result of fusion of preural centrum 1 with one or more adjacent ural centra.[TAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-08-14", external_class="TAO:0000158", ontology="TAO", source="TAO:wd", source="ZFIN:curator"}
property_value: external_definition "Rodlike caudal bony structure unique to anurans that lies within a compartment formed by the elongated, anteriorly oriented pelvic girdle. The urostyle is formed by the fusion of the coccyx and the hypochord.[AAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-06-20", external_class="AAO:0000732", ontology="AAO", source="AAO:Pugener_2002", source="AAO:Pugener_and_Maglia_2008"}
property_value: taxon_notes "In zebrafish, it is composed of preural vertebra 1 and ural centra 1 and 2. The number of ural centra that become fused with preural centrum 1 varies among teleost subgroups. Because of varying developmental origins the urostyle may not be homologous across species." xsd:string {source="TAO"}

[Term]
id: UBERON:0003107
name: Meckel's cartilage
def: "Meckel's cartilage is the bilaterally paired, rod-like, cartilaginous ventral component of the lower jar, or ventral mandibular arch. It is typically resorbed in adults." [PMID:3693112, Wikipedia:Meckel's_cartilage]
