[Term]
id: UBERON:0003142
name: prepupa
def: "An organism at the prepupal stage. The prepupal stage is a life stage interposed between the larval and the pupal stages in insects that undergo a complete metamorphosis. The start of the pre-pupal stage is marked by pupariation, and the end is marked by pupation." [GO:0035210]
xref: BTO:0001110
xref: HAO:0000812
is_a: UBERON:0000468 ! multicellular organism
relationship: immediate_transformation_of UBERON:0002548 ! larva
relationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:50557 ! Insecta

[Term]
id: UBERON:0003143
name: pupa
def: "An organism at the pupal stage. A life cycle stage of holometabolous insects in which the organism is a pupa and starts with the larval-pupal apolysis and ends with pupal-adult apolysis." [https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/issues/562, Wikipedia:Pupa]
