[Term]
id: UBERON:0003722
name: middle cranial fossa
def: "The compartment containing the anterior extremities and half the inferior surface of the temporal lobes (TEMPORAL LOBE) of the cerebral hemispheres. Lying posterior and inferior to the anterior cranial fossa (CRANIAL FOSSA, ANTERIOR), it is formed by part of the TEMPORAL BONE and SPHENOID BONE. It is separated from the posterior cranial fossa (CRANIAL FOSSA, POSTERIOR) by crests formed by the superior borders of the petrous parts of the temporal bones[MESH]. The middle fossa, deeper than the anterior cranial fossa, is narrow medially and widens laterally to the sides of the skull. It is separated from the posterior fossa by the clivus and the petrous crest. It is bounded in front by the posterior margins of the lesser wings of the sphenoid bone, the anterior clinoid processes, and the ridge forming the anterior margin of the chiasmatic groove; behind, by the superior angles of the petrous portions of the temporal bones and the dorsum sellC&; laterally by the temporal squamC&, sphenoidal angles of the parietals, and greater wings of the sphenoid. It is traversed by the squamosal, sphenoparietal, sphenosquamosal, and sphenopetrosal sutures[WP]." [MESH:A01.456.830.165, Wikipedia:Middle_cranial_fossa]
synonym: "fossa cranii media" RELATED OMO:0003011 [Wikipedia:Middle_cranial_fossa]
synonym: "middle fossa" BROAD [Wikipedia:Middle_cranial_fossa]
xref: FMA:54369
xref: GAID:84
xref: MESH:D035301
xref: NCIT:C33117
xref: UMLS:C0230045 {source="ncithesaurus:Middle_Fossa"}
xref: Wikipedia:Middle_cranial_fossa
