xref: Wikipedia:Ectomesenchyme
is_a: UBERON:0007213 {notes="consider merging"} ! mesenchyme derived from head neural crest
property_value: editor_note "consider merging with UBERON:0007213 mesenchyme derived from head neural crest" xsd:string
property_value: external_definition "Ectomesenchyme has similar properties to mesenchyme. The major difference is that ectomesenchyme is usually considered to arise from neural crest cells, which are a critical group of cells that form in the cranial region during early vertebrate development. Thus, ectomesenchyme plays a critical role in the formation of the hard and soft tissues of the head and neck such as bones, muscles, teeth, and, most important, the branchial arches[Wikipedia:Ectomesenchyme]." xsd:string {source="Wikipedia:Ectomesenchyme"}
property_value: external_definition "Portion of tissue that develops from the cranial neural crest and which cells populate a series of pharyngeal arches from which develops the support skeleton of the jaw and gills[ZFA:0005771]." xsd:string {source="ZFA:0005771"}

