relationship: part_of UBERON:0002167 ! right lung
property_value: taxon_notes "in humans, the right lung typically has 3 lobes (superior, middle, inferior). The lobar fissures are often incomplete, making a connection between two apposed lobes. Conversely, more than the expected number of lobes may be produced by new fissures e.g. the azygous lobe of the lung. The additional lobes are termed 'accessory lobes' -- http://www.gpnotebook.co.uk/simplepage.cfm?ID=1120927803" xsd:string
property_value: taxon_notes "In mouse this is sometimes divided into intermediate and diaphragmatic lobes" xsd:string {source="ISBN:0123813611"}

