[Term]
id: UBERON:0005412
name: optic fissure
def: "Groove that is in the developing ventral optic cup and through which blood vessels pass to the enclosed mesenchyme[ZFA]. a ventral fissure in the developing optic cup through which blood vessels pass to the enclosed mesenchyme[Free online medical dictionary]." [http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/optic+fissure, https://sourceforge.net/tracker/?func=detail&atid=440764&aid=3083162&group_id=36855, Wikipedia:Choroid_fissure, ZFA:0001284]
comment: Develeopment notes: As the eye starts to develop, a gap opens on the underside of each eye bud. This gap provides a way for the developing eye to be nourished. This gap, called the optic fissure, has to close before the eye is fully developed. Coloboma is the incomplete closer of the optic fissure
subset: pheno_slim
subset: vertebrate_core
synonym: "choroid fissure" RELATED [MA:0001305, XAO:0000474, ZFA:0001284]
synonym: "choroid fissure - optic fissure" EXACT [VHOG:0000655]
synonym: "optic fissures" EXACT OMO:0003004 [ZFA:0001284]
synonym: "optic stalk fissure" EXACT [EHDAA2:0001319]
synonym: "ventral choroidal fissure" RELATED [XAO:0000474]
