[Term]
id: UBERON:0005880
name: prepollex
def: "A rudimentary additional digit-like structure on the preaxial side of the thumb of certain amphibians and mammals[dictionary.com]." [http://dictionary.com]
comment: not homologous to digit 1 of tetrapods. Note we treat the prepollex as distinct from the digits, which are not part of the carpus
synonym: "pseudothumb" RELATED [DOI:10.1098/rsbl.2009.1038]
