[Term]
id: UBERON:0006216
name: cervical sinus of His
def: "A temporary depression caudal to the second pharyngeal arch, containing the succeeding pharyngeal arches; it is overgrown by the second pharyngeal arch and closes off as the cervical vesicle. This sinus is bounded in front by the hyoid arch, and behind by the thoracic wall." [http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/cervical+sinus, Wikipedia:Cervical_sinus]
subset: emapa_ehdaa2
subset: pheno_slim
synonym: "cervical sinus" EXACT [EHDAA2:0000078]
