[Term]
id: UBERON:0006378
name: strand of vibrissa hair
def: "A specialized hair usually employed for tactile sensation. Vibrissae hair grow around the nostrils, above the lips, and on other parts of the face of most mammals, and all primates except humans. vibrissae are different from other hairs because they are implanted in a special hair follicle incorporating a capsule of blood called a blood sinus and heavily innervated by sensory nerves[WP]." [https://sourceforge.net/tracker/?func=detail&aid=3213510&group_id=76834&atid=1205376, Wikipedia:Whiskers]
synonym: "contour hair" EXACT [MP:0009003]
synonym: "macrovibrissa" NARROW []
synonym: "microvibrissa" NARROW []
synonym: "motile vibrissa" NARROW []
synonym: "sinus hair" EXACT [EMAPA:26747, MP:0009003]
synonym: "tactile hair" RELATED []
synonym: "touch hair" EXACT [MP:0009003]
synonym: "true whisker" NARROW []
synonym: "vibrissa" RELATED []
synonym: "vibrissa hair" EXACT [MA:0000782]
synonym: "vibrissae" RELATED OMO:0003004 []
synonym: "whisker" NARROW [MA:0000163]
xref: BTO:0003488
xref: EMAPA:26747
xref: http://eulep.pdn.cam.ac.uk/~skinbase/Annotated_anatomy_of_the_mouse_vibrissa/vibrissa_labelled.jpg
xref: MA:0000782
xref: MESH:D014738
xref: Wikipedia:Whiskers
intersection_of: UBERON:0001037 ! strand of hair
intersection_of: part_of UBERON:0011933 ! vibrissa unit
disjoint_from: UBERON:0011931 ! nasal hair
relationship: capable_of_part_of GO:0050975 ! sensory perception of touch
relationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:40674 {source="Wikipedia"} ! Mammalia
relationship: never_in_taxon NCBITaxon:9606 {source="Skinbase"} ! Homo sapiens
property_value: taxon_notes "In harbor seals, the structure of the vibrissal shaft is undulated (wavy) and flattened. This specialization is also found in most true seals. In contrast, the whiskers of the California sea lion are circular or elliptical in cross-section and are smooth." xsd:string {source="Wikipedia:Hydrodynamic_reception#Species_differences_in_vibrissae"}

