[Term]
id: UBERON:0006530
name: seminal fluid
def: "A substance formed from the secretion of one or more glands of the male genital tract in which sperm cells are suspended." [http://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165]
synonym: "male genital fluid" RELATED []
synonym: "male genital secretion" RELATED []
synonym: "milt" NARROW [PMID:31287811, PMID:35203131] {comment="CURATOR NOTE A secretion from the glands of the male reproductive system in some aquatic animals that contains sperm and is sprayed onto the eggs."}
synonym: "seminal fluid" RELATED [BTO:0001232]
synonym: "seminal plasma" EXACT [BTO:0001232]
xref: BTO:0001232
xref: CALOHA:TS-0918
xref: EMAPA:36543
xref: FMA:62967
xref: MA:0002523
xref: MAT:0000057
xref: MIAA:0000057
intersection_of: UBERON:0000456 ! secretion of exocrine gland
intersection_of: part_of UBERON:0001968 ! semen
intersection_of: produced_by UBERON:0005399 ! male reproductive gland
relationship: capable_of_part_of GO:0048240 ! sperm capacitation
relationship: capable_of_part_of GO:1902093 ! positive regulation of flagellated sperm motility
property_value: curator_notes "this ontology contains a number of subtypes of seminal fluid, defined according to glands (which are more taxonomically restricted)" xsd:string
property_value: curator_notes "we follow FMA and make this class a generic superclass of the secretions of different glands (prostate, bulbo-urethreal, seminal vesicle). MA (and ncit) follows a mixture model, where these secretions are part of the seminal fluid" xsd:string
property_value: function_notes "seminal fluid may have a role in sperm capacitation, sperm motility" xsd:string
property_value: taxon_notes "This term covers a variety of species. Example: In D. melanogaster, seminal fluid proteins affect female receptivity, ovulation, oogenesis, sperm storage, sperm competition and mating plug formation" xsd:string {source="DOI:10.1046/j.1365-2540.2001.00961.x"}

