xref: SCTID:80391004
xref: Wikipedia:Ligamentum_venosum
is_a: UBERON:0006592 {source="FMA"} ! transformed vein
relationship: develops_from UBERON:0002083 ! ductus venosus
property_value: depiction "http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a3/Gray1087-liver.png" xsd:anyURI

[Term]
id: UBERON:0006588
name: round ligament of liver
def: "A degenerative string of tissue that exists in the free edge of the falciform ligament of the liver. Anatomically, the round ligament divides the left part of the liver into medial and lateral sections. The round ligament represents the remnant of the fetal left umbilical vein. The round ligament therefore only exists in mammals. Prenatally and for a month or two after birth, the left umbilical vein is patent, subsequently degenerating to fibrous tissue, the round ligament. The umbilical vein/round ligament inserts around the umbilicus and is an important landmark of the inner surface of the anterior abdominal wall[WP]." [Wikipedia:Round_ligament_of_liver]
synonym: "ligamentum teres" BROAD [Wikipedia:Round_ligament_of_liver]
synonym: "ligamentum teres hepatis" EXACT OMO:0003011 [FMA:14079, FMA:TA]
synonym: "ligamentum teres hepatitis" EXACT [Wikipedia:Round_ligament_of_liver]
synonym: "ligamentum teres of liver" EXACT [FMA:14079]
xref: FMA:14079
xref: MESH:D000069592
xref: NCIT:C34008
xref: SCTID:262209009
xref: UMLS:C0230247 {source="ncithesaurus:Round_Ligament_of_the_Liver"}
xref: Wikipedia:Round_ligament_of_liver
is_a: UBERON:0006592 ! transformed vein
is_a: UBERON:0013139 ! ligament of liver
disjoint_from: UBERON:0006589 ! round ligament of uterus
relationship: develops_from UBERON:0002066 ! umbilical vein
relationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:40674 {source="Wikipedia"} ! Mammalia

[Term]
id: UBERON:0006589
name: round ligament of uterus
def: "The round ligament of the uterus originates at the uterine horns, in the parametrium. It leaves the pelvis via the deep inguinal ring, passes through the inguinal canal and continues on to the labia majora where its fibers spread and mix with the tissue of the mons pubis[WP]. A fibromuscular band that attaches to the uterus and then passes along the broad ligament, out through the inguinal ring, and into the labium majus[MESH]." [MESH:A02.513.803, Wikipedia:Round_ligament_of_uterus]
synonym: "Hunter's ligament" EXACT [FMA:20420]
synonym: "ligamentum teres of uterus" EXACT []
synonym: "ligamentum teres uteri" EXACT [Wikipedia:Round_ligament_of_uterus]
