[Term]
id: UBERON:0006949
name: cervical loop
def: "The cervical loop is the location on an enamel organ in a developing tooth where the outer enamel epithelium and the inner enamel epithelium join. The cervical loop is a histologic term indicating a specific epithelial structure at the apical side of the tooth germ, consisting of loosely aggregated stellate reticulum in the center surrounded by stratum intermedium. These tissues are enveloped by a basal layer of epithelium known on the outside of the tooth as outer enamel epithelium and on the inside as inner enamel epithelium. During root formation the inner layers of epithelium disappear and only the basal layers are left creating Hertwig's Epithelial Root Sheath (HERS). At this point it is usually referred to as HERS instead of the cervical loop to indicate the structural difference[WP]." [Wikipedia:Cervical_loop]
xref: Wikipedia:Cervical_loop
is_a: UBERON:0003843 ! dental epithelium
relationship: continuous_with UBERON:0006951 ! inner dental epithelium
relationship: continuous_with UBERON:0006952 ! outer dental epithelium
relationship: part_of UBERON:0005176 ! tooth enamel organ

[Term]
id: UBERON:0006950
name: stellate reticulum
alt_id: UBERON:0007441
def: "The stellate reticulum is a group of cells located in the center of the enamel organ of a developing tooth. These cells are star shaped and synthesize glycosaminoglycans. As glycosamingoglycans are produced, water is drawn in between the cells and stretch them apart. As they are moved further away from one another, the stellate reticulum maintain contact with one another through desmosomes, resulting in their unique appearance. stellate reticulum is lost after the first layer of dentin is laid down. this brings cells in inner enamel epithelium closer to blood vessels at the periphery[WP]." [Wikipedia:Stellate_reticulum]
synonym: "reticulum stellatum" RELATED OMO:0003011 [Wikipedia:Stellate_reticulum]
xref: BTO:0003910
xref: NCIT:C33613
xref: UMLS:C1514963 {source="ncithesaurus:Stellate_Reticulum"}
xref: Wikipedia:Stellate_reticulum
is_a: UBERON:0003843 ! dental epithelium
relationship: capable_of GO:0006024 ! glycosaminoglycan biosynthetic process
relationship: part_of UBERON:0005176 {source="BTO", source="Wikipedia"} ! tooth enamel organ
relationship: part_of UBERON:0006949 ! cervical loop
