[Term]
id: UBERON:0007193
name: orbital gyrus
def: "The inferior or orbital surface of the frontal lobe is concave, and rests on the orbital plate of the frontal bone. It is divided into four orbital gyri by a well-marked H-shaped orbital sulcus. These are named, from their position, the medial, anterior, lateral, and posterior orbital gyri. The medial orbital gyrus presents a well-marked antero-posterior sulcus, the olfactory sulcus, for the olfactory tract; the portion medial to this is named the straight gyrus, and is continuous with the superior frontal gyrus on the medial surface." [Wikipedia:Orbital_gyri]
synonym: "gyrus orbitales" RELATED OMO:0003011 [Wikipedia:Orbital_gyri]
synonym: "orbital gyri" EXACT OMO:0003004 [Wikipedia:Orbital_gyri]
xref: BAMS:OrG
xref: FMA:256194
xref: neuronames:91
xref: SCTID:280372002
xref: Wikipedia:Orbital_gyri
is_a: UBERON:0000200 ! gyrus
relationship: part_of UBERON:0016525 ! frontal lobe
property_value: depiction "http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b1/Human_brainstem_anterior_view_2_description.JPG" xsd:anyURI

[Term]
id: UBERON:0007194
name: vesicular gland
def: "The vesicular gland is part of the male reproductive system. The vesicular gland contributes fluids, energy substrates, and buffers to semen. It can be found near the Coagulating gland, which also belongs to the reproductive system." [BTO:0003717]
