[Term]
id: UBERON:0007315
name: internal pudendal artery
def: "The internal pudendal artery is an artery that branches off the internal iliac artery, providing blood to the external genitalia. The internal pudendal artery is the terminal branch of the anterior trunk of the internal iliac artery. It is smaller in the female than in the male." [Wikipedia:Internal_pudendal_artery]
synonym: "arteria pudenda interna" EXACT OMO:0003011 [Wikipedia:Internal_pudendal_artery]
synonym: "arteriae pudendae interna" EXACT OMO:0003011 [doi:10.1002/ca.23705]
synonym: "arteriae pudendales interna" EXACT OMO:0003011 [doi:10.1002/ca.23705]
synonym: "internal pudendal vessels" BROAD [Wikipedia:Internal_pudendal_artery]
synonym: "internal pudic artery" EXACT [Wikipedia:Internal_pudendal_artery]
xref: FMA:18835
xref: SCTID:244309002
xref: Wikipedia:Internal_pudendal_artery
