[Term]
id: UBERON:0007693
name: caroticotympanic artery
def: "The caroticotympanic branch (tympanic branch) is small; it enters the tympanic cavity through a minute foramen in the carotid canal, and anastomoses with the anterior tympanic branch of the internal maxillary, and with the stylomastoid artery." [Wikipedia:Caroticotympanic_arteries]
synonym: "arteriae caroticotympanicae" RELATED OMO:0003011 [Wikipedia:Caroticotympanic_arteries]
synonym: "caroticotympanic branch" RELATED [Wikipedia:Caroticotympanic_arteries]
