[Term]
id: UBERON:0008260
name: spine appendage
def: "A hard, thorny or needle-like structure which occurs on various animals. Animals such as porcupines and sea urchins grow spines as a self-defense mechanism. Spines are often formed of keratin. Other animals with spines are hedgehogs, spiny mice and at least two ornithischian dinosaurs." [Wikipedia:Spine_(zoology)]
subset: grouping_class
