[Term]
id: UBERON:0008446
name: flexor pollicis longus muscle
def: "A muscle in the forearm and hand that flexes the thumb. It lies in the same plane as the flexor digitorum profundus." [Wikipedia:Flexor_pollicis_longus_muscle]
synonym: "flexor pollicis" RELATED [Wikipedia:Flexor_pollicis_longus_muscle]
synonym: "flexor pollicis longus" RELATED [Wikipedia:Flexor_pollicis_longus_muscle]
synonym: "flexor pollicis muscle" RELATED [Wikipedia:Flexor_pollicis_longus_muscle]
synonym: "musculus flexor pollicis longus" RELATED OMO:0003011 [Wikipedia:Flexor_pollicis_longus_muscle]
xref: FMA:38481
xref: SCTID:361818001
xref: Wikipedia:Flexor_pollicis_longus_muscle
is_a: UBERON:0014892 ! skeletal muscle organ, vertebrate
relationship: has_muscle_antagonist UBERON:0003234 {source="dbpedia"} ! extensor pollicis longus muscle
relationship: has_muscle_insertion UBERON:0004444 {notes="The base of the distal phalanx of the thumb", source="dbpedia"} ! proximal epiphysis of distal phalanx of manual digit 1
relationship: has_muscle_origin UBERON:0001423 {notes="The middle 2/4 of the volar surface of the radius and the adjacent interosseus membrane.", source="dbpedia"} ! radius bone
relationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:9606 {source="Wikipedia"} ! Homo sapiens
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002386 ! forelimb zeugopod
property_value: depiction "http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/72/FPL.png" xsd:anyURI
property_value: taxon_notes "Modern humans are unique among hominids in having a flexor pollicis longus (FPL) muscle belly that is separate from that of the flexor digitorum profundus (FDP). While the FPL is not a separate muscle belly in extant great apes, a distinct tendon from the FDP belly might be present. In some individuals this tendon tend to act more like a ligament which restricts extension of the interphalangeal joint of the thumb. In orangutans there is a tendon similar in insertion and function to the FPL in humans, but which has an intrinsic origin on the oblique head of the adductor pollicis" xsd:string {source="WP"}

[Term]
id: UBERON:0008447
name: intertarsal joint
def: "Intertarsal articulations are the joints of the tarsus. The specific intertarsal articulations are: Talocalcaneal articulation Talocalcaneonavicular articulation Calcaneocuboid articulation Cuneonavicular articulation Cuboideonavicular articulation Intercuneiform articulation Cuneocuboid articulation." [Wikipedia:Intertarsal_articulations]
