[Term]
id: UBERON:0008523
name: infrahyoid muscle
def: "The infrahyoid muscles are a group of four pairs of muscles in the anterior part of the neck. (The term infrahyoid refers to the region below to the hyoid bone in the neck. ) Collectively, they are referred to as the strap muscles, because the muscles are long and flat much like a strap." [Wikipedia:Infrahyoid_muscles]
