[Term]
id: UBERON:0008857
name: stomach smooth muscle circular layer
def: "The middle layer of the muscularis; it is continuous with the circular layer of the esophagus, but is absent in the fundus and lies concentric to the longitudinal axis of the stomach; the circular layer is normally tonically constricted forming a functional pyloric sphincter, which controls the movement of chyme into the duodenum." [MP:0010780]
