[Term]
id: UBERON:0008888
name: vesical venous plexus
def: "The vesical plexus envelops the lower part of the bladder and the base of the prostate and communicates with the pudendal and prostatic plexuses. It is drained, by means of several vesical veins, into the hypogastric veins." [Wikipedia:Vesical_venous_plexus]
synonym: "plexus venosus vesicalis" RELATED OMO:0003011 [Wikipedia:Vesical_venous_plexus]
