[Term]
id: UBERON:0008962
name: forelimb bone
def: "A bone that is part of a forelimb region. Examples: humerus, any of the phalanges. Counter-example: scapula (a bone of the pectoral girdle). Note that we consider the forelimb to end at the shoulder." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165]
