intersection_of: UBERON:0000982 ! skeletal joint
intersection_of: connects UBERON:0003656 ! mesopodium bone
intersection_of: connects UBERON:0004302 ! proximal phalanx
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002544 ! digit
property_value: editor_note "We include these joints as being part of the digits; this is consistent with the FMA, and makes classification easier. Note that digit and metapodial regions are part-disjoint" xsd:string

[Term]
id: UBERON:0009563
name: pastern region of limb
def: "A part of the leg of a horse between the fetlock and the top of the hoof. It incorporates the long pastern bone (proximal phalanx) and the short pastern bone (middle phalanx), which are held together by two sets of paired ligaments to form the pastern joint (proximal interphalangeal joint)." [Wikipedia:Pastern]
xref: SCTID:370725009
xref: Wikipedia:Pastern
is_a: UBERON:0002529 ! limb segment
relationship: part_of UBERON:0006050 ! digit 3
property_value: editor_note "in future this may be merged into a more species-neutral class for the distal and medial segments of a digit." xsd:string

