[Term]
id: UBERON:0009986
name: lateral epicondyle of femur
def: "The lateral epicondyle of the femur, smaller and less prominent than the medial epicondyle, gives attachment to the fibular collateral ligament of the knee-joint. Directly below it is a small depression from which a smooth well-marked groove curves obliquely upward and backward to the posterior extremity of the condyle." [Wikipedia:Lateral_epicondyle_of_the_femur]
synonym: "e. lateralis femoris" RELATED OMO:0003011 [Wikipedia:Lateral_epicondyle_of_the_femur]
synonym: "epicondylus lateralis (femur)" EXACT [FMA:32867]
