[Term]
id: UBERON:0010019
name: spiracle (sensu Vertebrata)
def: "A small hole behind each eye that opens to the mouth in some fish. In the primitive jawless fish the first gill opening immediately behind the mouth is essentially similar to the other gill openings." [ISBN:0073040584, Wikipedia:Spiracle#Vertebrates]
synonym: "spiracle" BROAD SENSU [NCBITaxon:7742]
synonym: "vertebrate spiracle" EXACT []
xref: Wikipedia:Spiracle#Vertebrates
is_a: UBERON:0003102 {source="cjm"} ! surface structure
relationship: develops_from UBERON:0004362 ! pharyngeal arch 1
relationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:7742 ! Vertebrata <vertebrates>
relationship: never_in_taxon NCBITaxon:32523 ! Tetrapoda
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001004 ! respiratory system
relationship: present_in_taxon NCBITaxon:119203 ! Selachii
property_value: external_ontology_notes "GO term spiracle morphogenesis, open tracheal system - does not refer to this structure" xsd:string {isAbout="GO:0035277"}
property_value: taxon_notes "In elasmobranchs (sharks and rays), a spiracle is found behind each eye, and is often used to pump water through the gills while the animal is at rest (Fouts, 2003). A spiracle is also found in primitive bony fishes as the chirrups." xsd:string
property_value: taxon_notes "The spiracle is still found in all cartilaginous fish except chimaeras, and in bony fishes in the coelacanth, sturgeon, paddlefish and bichirs. It is also seen as an otic notch in the skull of the extinct labyrinthodonts, and is thought to be associated with the ear opening in amniotes and frogs" xsd:string {source="WP"}

[Term]
id: UBERON:0010020
name: tubotympanic recess epithelium
def: "The dorsal portion of the embryonic first endodermal pharyngeal pouch; it develops into the middle ear cavity." [ISBN:0124020607, VHOG:0001297]
synonym: "tubotympanic recess" RELATED [VHOG:0001297]
xref: EHDAA2:0004115
