[Term]
id: UBERON:0010048
name: Duvernoy's gland
def: "A gland situated on the upper lip posterior to the eye, found in non-venomous snakes. Releases secretion via duct adjacent to posterior maxillary teeth." [http://public.wsu.edu/~kkardong/Web%20of%20KVK_06b/Publications/reptile%20glands.pdf, ISBN:0073040584, UBERON:cjm, Wikipedia:Duvernoy's_gland]
comment: positioned posterior to the eye, encased in a thin cover of connective tissue, and consists mostly of serous cells. A single, short duct extends anteromedially from the lumen of the gland to the base of the posterior fangs.[WP]
xref: Wikipedia:Duvernoy's_gland
