relationship: part_of UBERON:0001776 {source="ZFA"} ! optic choroid
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002200 {source="XAO"} ! vasculature of head
property_value: editor_note "Consider merging with capillary layer. Consider choriocapillaris complex" xsd:string
property_value: external_definition "A plexus of capillaries that is located anteromedial to the eye. It is a capillary layer in the choroid. It is in contact with the basal surface of the retinal pigmented epithelium and supplies the photoreceptors with oxygen and nutrients. The fused basement membrane of this capillary layer and the pigmented epithelium is called Bruchs's membrane.[XAO:0004176]." xsd:string {source="XAO:0004176"}
property_value: external_definition "Is an ocular vasculature that develops adjacent to the pigment epithelium of the eye. The optic choroid vascular plexus develops from the primitive mesencephalic artery. Initially blood enters from the mesencephalic central artery, and the dorsal ciliary vein. The plexus drains via the ophthalmic vein. The plexus supplies blood to the retina[ZFA:0005094]." xsd:string {source="ZFA:0005094"}
property_value: taxon_notes "The choroid of teleosts is a connective tissue layer rich in blood vessels, and one or two choroidal glands." xsd:string {source="PMID:14738502"}

