[Term]
id: UBERON:0010249
name: posterior meningeal artery
def: "The posterior meningeal artery are small vessels which are branches of the ascending pharyngeal artery which supply the dura mater. It passes through the mastoid foramen before entering the cranium via the jugular foramen." [Wikipedia:Posterior_meningeal_artery]
synonym: "arteria meningea posterior" RELATED OMO:0003011 [Wikipedia:Posterior_meningeal_artery]
synonym: "meningeal branches of the ascending pharyngeal artery" RELATED [Wikipedia:Posterior_meningeal_artery]
