[Term]
id: UBERON:0010308
name: os opticus
def: "Scleral element located at the posterior pole of the scleral cartilage surrounding the foramen through which the optic nerve fibers pass. the internal architecture of this bone reveals a cancellous marrow cavity with fatty tissue." [PMID:16496288]
