[Term]
id: UBERON:0010515
name: brille
def: "A layer of transparent, immovable disc-shaped skin or scale covering the eyes of some animals for protection, especially in animals without eyelids. The brille has evolved from a fusion of the upper and lower eyelids." [Wikipedia:Brille]
comment: there are transitional stages between total lid loss and full brille formation (Bellairs & Boyd, 1947).
synonym: "eye cap" RELATED []
synonym: "ocular scale" RELATED []
xref: Wikipedia:Brille
is_a: UBERON:0000014 ! zone of skin
relationship: has_fused_element UBERON:0001712 ! upper eyelid
relationship: has_fused_element UBERON:0001713 ! lower eyelid
relationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:32561 ! Sauria
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000019 ! camera-type eye
property_value: taxon_notes "In snakes, there is no eyelid and the brille is clear and cannot be distinguished except when the animal is becoming ready for ecdysis. At that time, it becomes cloudy and is visible as a cover over the eye. When the snake moults, the brille is also shed as part of its skin. The Brilles protect their eyes from dust and dirt and gives them a 'glassy-eyed' blank appearance Snakes, flap-footed lizards, night lizards, and some skinks have brilles. All geckos except those in the subfamily Eublepharinae (eyelid geckos) possess brilles. Fish also have transparent eyelids called adipose eyelids." xsd:string

[Term]
id: UBERON:0010516
name: clasper
def: "A male anatomical structure found some groups of animals, used in mating. Male cartilaginous fish have claspers formed from the posterior portion of their pelvic fin which serve as intromittent organs used to channel semen into the female's cloaca during mating. The act of mating in some fish including sharks usually includes one of the claspers raised to allow water into the siphon through a specific orifice. The clasper is then inserted into the vagina, where it opens like an umbrella to anchor its position. The siphon then begins to contract expelling water and sperm. Male chimaeras have cephalic claspers on their heads, which are thought to aid in holding the female during mating." [Wikipedia:clasper]
xref: Wikipedia:clasper
is_a: UBERON:0008811 {source="Wikipedia"} ! intromittent organ
relationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:7777 ! Chondrichthyes
property_value: taxon_notes "the term is also used for insect claspers, but we reserve it for the elasmobranchii structure" xsd:string

[Term]
id: UBERON:0010517
name: cephalic clasper
def: "A mace-like spiny-headed rod found on the mid-dorsal surface of heads of male Holocephali. Thought to aid in holding the female during copulation." [http://fishbase.org/glossary/Glossary.php?q=tenaculum, http://www.fishbase.org/glossary/Glossary.php?q=cephalic+clasper, Wikipedia:Chimaera#Description_and_tastes]
synonym: "anterior tenaculum" RELATED []
synonym: "head clasper" RELATED [http://www.fishbase.org/glossary/Glossary.php?q=head+clasper]
synonym: "tenaculum" RELATED []
xref: Wikipedia:Chimaera#Description_and_tastes
intersection_of: UBERON:0010516 ! clasper
intersection_of: part_of UBERON:0000033 ! head
relationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:7864 ! Chimaeriformes
relationship: intersects_midsagittal_plane_of UBERON:0000033 ! head

[Term]
id: UBERON:0010518
name: pelvic fin clasper
def: "The rod-like extension of the medial portion of the pelvic fin in male Elasmobranchii and Holocephali. Claspers are used as intromittent organs (not in clasping), the grooves on their facing surfaces together forming a tube for the transmission of sperm when the claspers are held together. The anterior proximal opening is called the apopyle, the posterior distal opening the rhipidion." [http://fishbase.org/Glossary/Glossary.php?q=clasper]
synonym: "clasper" RELATED []
synonym: "myxopterygium" EXACT [http://fishbase.org/Glossary/Glossary.php?q=clasper]
intersection_of: UBERON:0010516 ! clasper
intersection_of: part_of UBERON:0000152 ! pelvic fin

