[Term]
id: UBERON:0010747
name: body of ilium
def: "The body of ilium enters into the formation of the acetabulum, of which it forms rather less than two-fifths. Its external surface is partly articular, partly non-articular; the articular segment forms part of the lunate surface of the acetabulum, the non-articular portion contributes to the acetabular fossa. The internal surface of the body is part of the wall of the lesser pelvis and gives origin to some fibers of the Obturator internus. Below, it is continuous with the pelvic surfaces of the ischium and pubis, only a faint line indicating the place of union." [Wikipedia:Body_of_ilium]
subset: pheno_slim
synonym: "corpus ossis ilii" RELATED OMO:0003011 [Wikipedia:Body_of_ilium]
synonym: "ilium body" EXACT [FMA:42825]
xref: FMA:42825
xref: SCTID:292524005
xref: Wikipedia:Body_of_ilium
is_a: UBERON:0005913 {source="FMA"} ! zone of bone organ
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001273 ! ilium

