property_value: curator_notes "over time, the synapsids' quadrate-articular jaw joint (which the rest of the tetrapods possess) was replaced by a dentary-squamosal joint (which all living mammals possess), while the quadrate and articular migrated, shrank, and became part of the complex of middle ear bones." xsd:string {source="http://evolution.berkeley.edu/evolibrary/article/evograms_05"}
