[Term]
id: UBERON:0011183
name: corpus spongiosum of penis
def: "Corpus spongiosum (also known as corpus cavernosum urethrae in older texts) is the mass of spongy tissue surrounding the male urethra within the penis." [Wikipedia:Corpus_spongiosum_penis]
synonym: "corpus cavernosum urethra" RELATED DEPRECATED [Wikipedia:Corpus_spongiosum_penis]
synonym: "corpus cavernosum urethrae" RELATED DEPRECATED [Wikipedia:Corpus_spongiosum_penis]
synonym: "corpus spongiosum" RELATED [Wikipedia:Corpus_spongiosum_penis]
synonym: "spongiose body of penis" EXACT [FMA:19617]
xref: FMA:19617
xref: NCIT:C32384
xref: SCTID:279712008
xref: UMLS:C1522442 {source="ncithesaurus:Corpus_Spongiosum"}
xref: Wikipedia:Corpus_spongiosum_penis
is_a: UBERON:0008324 ! erectile tissue
relationship: capable_of_part_of GO:0043084 ! penile erection
relationship: part_of UBERON:0000989 ! penis
relationship: surrounds UBERON:0000057 ! urethra
property_value: depiction "http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f6/Gray1155.png" xsd:anyURI
property_value: function_notes "The function of the corpus spongiosum in erection is to prevent the urethra from pinching closed, thereby maintaining the urethra as a viable channel for ejaculation. To do this, the corpus spongiosum remains pliable during erection while the corpora cavernosum penis becomes engorged with blood." xsd:string {source="WP"}

