[Term]
id: UBERON:0011186
name: Krause's gland
def: "Small, mucous accessory lacrimal glands that are found underneath the eyelid where the upper and lower conjuctivae meet. Their ducts unite into a rather long sinus which open into the fornix conjunctiva. There are approximately forty Krause glands in the region of the upper eyelid, and around 6 to 8 in the region of the lower lid. The function of these glands are to produce tears which are secreted onto the surface of the conjuctiva." [Wikipedia:Krause's_glands]
synonym: "accessory lacrimal gland" BROAD [FMA:59056]
synonym: "conjunctival gland" BROAD [FMA:59056]
synonym: "Krause gland" EXACT [FMA:59056]
