[Term]
id: UBERON:0011508
name: sphincter colli superficialis muscle
def: "The sphincter colli superficialis is composed of transverse muscle fibers, and covers the entire area between the lower jaw and chest. The muscle is used to tighten the skin on the underside of the throat." [Wikipedia:Platysma]
