[Term]
id: UBERON:0011510
name: cloacal bursa
def: "An evagination of the cloaca. In Testudines these are hypothesized to function in different physiological roles, primarily in respiration." [PMID:11479904, UBERON:cjm]
comment: Taxon notes: in cryptodires, bursae apparently function primarily in buoyancy control and secondarily in ion transport and nesting, but several pleurodires have been shown recently to use them in aquatic respiration.[PMID:11479904]
