[Term]
id: UBERON:0011622
name: thyrohyoid bone
def: "Is a laterally bowed, sagittally compressed, slender element that extends from dorsocaudally from the lateral parts of the basihyoid. It connects the basiohyoid with the rostral corner of the thyroid cartlilage of the larynx." [MURDOCH:1951]
