id: UBERON:0011635
name: splenial bone
def: "The splenial is a small bone in the lower jaw of reptiles, amphibians and birds, usually located on the lingual side (closest to the tongue) between the angular and suprangular." [Wikipedia:Splenial]
synonym: "splenial" EXACT [AAO:0000573]
