[Term]
id: UBERON:0011653
name: diapophysis of neural arch
def: "Paired processes that arise near the midpoint of the neural arch lamina, for the attachment of the tuberculum of two-headed ribs. Also called transverse processes. In anurans, the term diapophysis is used in reference to the modified transverse processes of the sacral vertebra elaborated for support of the pelvic girdle." [AAO:0000706]
synonym: "diapophysis" BROAD [AAO:0000706]
synonym: "transverse process" BROAD [AAO:0000706]
xref: AAO:0000706
is_a: UBERON:0004529 {source="AAO"} ! anatomical projection
relationship: connected_to UBERON:0011652 ! dorsal head of rib
relationship: part_of UBERON:0003861 {source="ISBN:0073040584"} ! neural arch
property_value: editor_note "taken from AAO, requires attention of amphibian anatomy experts, in particular, relationship to transverse processes" xsd:string

[Term]
id: UBERON:0011655
name: interclavicle
def: "Dermal bone of pectoral girdle that is median and ventral in position." [GO_REF:0000034, http://dx.plos.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0051070, VSAO:0000161]
synonym: "interclavicle bone" EXACT [http://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165]
xref: VSAO:0000161
xref: Wikipedia:Interclavicle
is_a: UBERON:0008907 {source="VSAO"} ! dermal bone
relationship: never_in_taxon NCBITaxon:32525 ! Theria <mammals>
relationship: part_of UBERON:0007831 {source="VSAO"} ! pectoral girdle skeleton
relationship: part_of UBERON:0007841 {gci_relation="part_of", gci_filler="NCBITaxon:8782"} ! furcula
relationship: present_in_taxon NCBITaxon:9257 ! Ornithorhynchus
property_value: editor_note "See discussion on pectoral girdles - change relationship to overlaps? Kardong: enlarged oval scale" xsd:string
property_value: taxon_notes "Present in therapids and monotremes, reduced in size in marsupials and placentals. In birds, the interclavicle is fused with the clavicles to form the furcula (wishbone); the furcula forms a 'Y' shape and the interclavicle is the stem of the 'Y'." xsd:string

