[Term]
id: UBERON:0013135
name: interdental plate
def: "The interdental plate refers to the bone-filled mesial-distal region between the teeth." [Wikipedia:Interdental_plate]
xref: Wikipedia:Interdental_plate
intersection_of: UBERON:0005913 ! zone of bone organ
intersection_of: located_in UBERON:0012111 ! diastema
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001708 ! jaw skeleton
property_value: taxon_notes "In paleobiology, the presence or absence of the interdental plate can determine the place of an animal in the evolutionary scale, and paleontologists use the interdental plate when trying to classify a new specimen. Thecodont reptiles and theropod dinosaur fossils have an interdental plate, whereas acrodont reptiles such as Sphenodontia do not.[3] Its presence in Archaeopteryx, an extinct avian, resulted in the proposal of the dinosaur-bird connection" xsd:string {source="WP"}

