[Term]
id: UBERON:0013153
name: arachnoid villus
def: "Small protrusions of the arachnoid mater into vascular sinuses, acting as one-way pressure-sensitive valves." [ISBN:0471888893, Wikipedia:Arachnoid_granulation]
synonym: "arachnoid granulations" RELATED [Wikipedia:Arachnoid_granulation]
synonym: "arachnoid villi" RELATED OMO:0003004 [Wikipedia:Arachnoid_granulation]
synonym: "arachnoid villus" RELATED [Wikipedia:Arachnoid_granulation]
synonym: "arachnoidal granulations" RELATED [Wikipedia:Arachnoid_granulation]
synonym: "glandulae pacchioni" RELATED [Wikipedia:Arachnoid_granulation]
synonym: "glandulæ pacchioni" RELATED [Wikipedia:Arachnoid_granulation]
synonym: "granulationes arachnoideales" RELATED [Wikipedia:Arachnoid_granulation]
synonym: "pacchioni's granulations" RELATED [Wikipedia:Arachnoid_granulation]
synonym: "pacchionian bodies" RELATED [Wikipedia:Arachnoid_granulation]
synonym: "pacchionian glands" RELATED [Wikipedia:Arachnoid_granulation]
synonym: "paccini's granulation" RELATED [Wikipedia:Arachnoid_granulation]
xref: FMA:83980
xref: NCIT:C32137
xref: UMLS:C0228130 {source="ncithesaurus:Arachnoid_Villus"}
xref: Wikipedia:Arachnoid_granulation
is_a: UBERON:0004529 ! anatomical projection
relationship: part_of UBERON:0002362 {source="FMA"} ! arachnoid mater
property_value: external_definition "Arachnoid granulations (or arachnoid villi) are small protrusions of the arachnoid (the thin second layer covering the brain) through the dura mater (the thick outer layer). They protrude into the venous sinuses of the brain, and allow cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) to exit the brain, and enter the blood stream. Largest granulations lie along the superior sagittal sinus, a large venous space running from front to back along the centre of the head (on the inside of the skull). They are, however, present along other dural sinuses as well. Smaller granulations are called villi, large calcified ones are referred to as pacchionian bodies[Wikipedia:Arachnoid_granulation]." xsd:string {source="Wikipedia:Arachnoid_granulation"}

