[Term]
id: UBERON:0013488
name: panniculus adiposus
def: "The panniculus adiposus is the fatty layer of the subcutaneous tissues, superficial to a deeper vestigial layer of muscle, the panniculus carnosus. An example is the Fascia of Camper. Another example is the superficial cervical fascia[WP]." [Wikipedia:Panniculus_adiposus]
