property_value: editor_note "It includes structures that are considered fascia by some sources but not by others. Consider merging with subcutaneous adipose tissue" xsd:string

[Term]
id: UBERON:0013489
name: superficial cervical fascia
def: "Superficial cervical fascia is a thin layer of subcutaneous connective tissue that lies between the dermis of the skin and the deep cervical fascia. It contains the platysma, cutaneous nerves, blood, and lymphatic vessels. It also contains a varying amount of fat, which is its distinguishing characteristic." [Wikipedia:Superficial_cervical_fascia]
comment: It is considered by some to be a part of the Panniculus adiposus, and not true fascia[WP]
synonym: "lamina superficialis fasciae cervicalis" EXACT OMO:0003011 [FMA:57805, FMA:TA]
synonym: "superficial cervical fascia" EXACT [FMA:57805]
synonym: "superficial layer of cervical fascia" EXACT [FMA:57805]
synonym: "superficial layer of deep cervical fascia" EXACT [FMA:57805]
xref: FMA:57805
xref: SCTID:175208005
xref: Wikipedia:Superficial_cervical_fascia
