[Term]
id: UBERON:0014690
name: left gastric vein
def: "The Left gastric vein (or coronary vein) carries blood low in Oxygen, tributaries derived from both surfaces of the stomach; it runs from right to left along the lesser curvature of the stomach, between the two layers of the lesser omentum, to the esophageal opening of the stomach, where it receives some esophageal veins. It then turns backward and passes from left to right behind the omental bursa and drains into the portal vein. Esophageal and paraesophageal varices are primarily supplied by the left gastric vein and typically drain into the azygos/hemiazygos venous system." [Wikipedia:Left_gastric_vein]
synonym: "coronary vein" RELATED [Wikipedia:Left_gastric_vein]
synonym: "vena gastrica sinistra" EXACT OMO:0003011 [Wikipedia:Left_gastric_vein]
xref: FMA:15399
xref: SCTID:281061005
xref: Wikipedia:Left_gastric_vein
intersection_of: UBERON:0004450 ! gastric vein
intersection_of: in_left_side_of UBERON:0002100 ! trunk
property_value: implements_design_pattern "https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/wiki/Modeling-paired-structures-Design-Pattern" xsd:anyURI

[Term]
id: UBERON:0014691
name: right gastric vein
def: "The right gastric vein, also known as the pyloric vein, drains blood from the lesser curvature of the stomach into the hepatic portal vein. It is part of the portal circulation." [Wikipedia:Right_gastric_vein]
synonym: "pyloric vein" RELATED [Wikipedia:Right_gastric_vein]
synonym: "vena gastrica dextra" EXACT OMO:0003011 [Wikipedia:Right_gastric_vein]
