[Term]
id: UBERON:0018650
name: annelid peristomium
def: "The peristomium is the second body segment in an annelid worm's body in the anterior end. It is directly behind the prostomium and contains the mouth, tentacular cirri, and sometimes feeding palps, which may instead occur on the prostomium. If an eversible pharynx is present, it is contained in this segment as well, and can fill up to 20 segments when inverted, depending on the species." [Wikipedia:Peristomium]
synonym: "peristomium" BROAD [Wikipedia:Peristomium]
xref: Wikipedia:Peristomium
is_a: UBERON:0000914 ! organismal segment
relationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:6340 {source="Wikipedia"} ! Annelida

[Term]
id: UBERON:0018651
name: foramen lacerum
def: "A triangular hole in the base of the skull located at the base of the medial pterygoid plate." [Wikipedia:Foramen_lacerum]
xref: FMA:54809
xref: SCTID:369444009
xref: Wikipedia:Foramen_lacerum
is_a: UBERON:0013685 {source="FMA"} ! foramen of skull
property_value: terminology_notes "For comparative reasons this term can only be used for the opening between the Os temporale, Os basisphenoidale, and Os occipitale (formerly the Foramen lacerum orale of the pig and horse). That which was formerly called Foramen lacerum aborale is the Foramen jugulare [NOMINA ANATOMICA VETERINARIA (2005)]" xsd:string

[Term]
id: UBERON:0018652
name: maxillary recess
def: "A hollow space in the skull of carnivores, which do not exhibit a maxillary sinus." [http://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165]
synonym: "recessus maxillaris" EXACT OMO:0003011 []
is_a: UBERON:0000464 ! anatomical space
relationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:33554 ! Carnivora
relationship: part_of UBERON:0003129 ! skull
property_value: editor_note "consider adding grouping with maxillary sinus" xsd:string
property_value: location_notes "Bounded medially by the Lamina orbitalis of the Os ethmoidale and laterally by the Maxilla and Os palatinum and in the dog also by the Os lacrimale[NOMINA ANATOMICA VETERINARIA (2005)]" xsd:string

[Term]
id: UBERON:0018653
name: anterior ethmoidal foramen
def: "The anterior ethmoidal foramen, situated about the middle of the lateral margin of the olfactory groove, transmits the anterior ethmoidal vessels and the anterior ethmoidal nerve; the nerve runs in a groove along the lateral edge of the cribriform plate to the slit-like opening above mentioned." [Wikipedia:Anterior_ethmoidal_foramen]
synonym: "foramina ethmoidalia anterius" EXACT OMO:0003011 []
xref: FMA:53135
xref: Wikipedia:Anterior_ethmoidal_foramen
is_a: UBERON:0013685 {source="FMA"} ! foramen of skull
disjoint_from: UBERON:0018654 {source="lexical"} ! posterior ethmoidal foramen

[Term]
id: UBERON:0018654
name: posterior ethmoidal foramen
def: "The posterior ethmoidal foramen opens at the back part of this margin under cover of the projecting lamina of the sphenoid, and transmits the posterior ethmoidal vessels and nerve." [Wikipedia:Posterior_ethmoidal_foramen]
synonym: "foramina ethmoidalia posterius" EXACT OMO:0003011 []
xref: FMA:53136
xref: Wikipedia:Posterior_ethmoidal_foramen
is_a: UBERON:0013685 {source="FMA"} ! foramen of skull

[Term]
id: UBERON:0018655
name: pars endotympanica
def: "This is present in the cat and forms the large medial part of the Bulla tympanica. It is not to be regarded as a part of the pars tympanica, which ossifies directly from connective tissue, whereas the Pars endotympanica is preformed in cartilage. The Septum bullae in the cat is formed by the Pars tympanica as well as by the Pars endotympanica(NOMINA ANATOMICA VETERINARIA (2005))." [http://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165]
is_a: UBERON:0005913 ! zone of bone organ
relationship: part_of UBERON:0013190 ! entotympanic bone

[Term]
id: UBERON:0018656
name: puparium
def: "A chitin-based cuticular shell derived from the cuticle of the final larval instar that surrounds the pupal form of the organism." [Wikipedia:Pupa#Puparium]
synonym: "puparia" RELATED OMO:0003004 []
is_a: UBERON:0001001 {source="FBbt"} ! chitin-based cuticle
relationship: develops_from UBERON:0002548 ! larva
relationship: surrounds UBERON:0003143 ! pupa

[Term]
id: UBERON:0018657
name: pupal case
def: "Any acellular shell or covering that surrounds the pupal form of an insect." [http://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165]
subset: grouping_class
intersection_of: UBERON:0000476 ! acellular anatomical structure
intersection_of: surrounds UBERON:0003143 ! pupa

[Term]
id: UBERON:0018663
name: recessus basilaris
def: "An opening of the otic duct within the inner ear. The recessus basilaris can open to the saccule (in frogs) or the lagena (in salamanders and caecilians). The sensory epithelium of the recessus basilaris is the basilar papilla (or papilla basilaris). Reference: Lewis, E.R. and R.E. Lombard. 1988. The amphibian inner ear. Pp. 93-123 in Fritszch, B., et al. (eds.), The Evolution of the Amphibian Auditory System. Wiley & Sons. [curated by D. Blackburn]." [PHENOSCAPE:wd]
synonym: "basilar papillar recess" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0000064 ! organ part
relationship: never_in_taxon NCBITaxon:40674 ! Mammalia
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001846 ! internal ear

