[Term]
id: UBERON:0035609
name: outer root sheath companion layer
def: "The innermost layer of the outer root sheath." [http://www.keratin.com/aa/aa022.shtml#03]
xref: BTO:0003970
is_a: UBERON:0004923 ! organ component layer
relationship: part_of UBERON:0005942 {source="BTO"} ! hair outer root sheath
property_value: structure_notes "It contains cells that are morphologically and biochemically different from the inner root sheath and outer root sheath. The cells of the companion layer are more flattened than the other cells of the outer root sheath and do not contain glycogen. In addition, a novel human type II cytokeratin, K6hf, is specifically expressed in the companion layer of the hair follicle" xsd:string

