[Term]
id: UBERON:0036144
name: incisive duct
def: "An infrequent rudimentary duct, or protrusion of the mucous membrane into the incisive canal, on either side of the anterior extremity of the nasal crest." [http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/incisive+duct]
comment: Taxon notes notes: In domestic mammals the Ductus incisivus is considerably better developed than in man. It is not accommodated in a Canalis incisivus, as in man, but in the Fissura palatina[NOMINA ANATOMICA VETERINARIA (2005)]
synonym: "ductus incisivus" EXACT OMO:0003011 [FMA:TA]
