[Term]
id: UBERON:0036177
name: nucleus recessus
def: "The fish catecholamines originate in two large aggregations of neurons: the nucleus recessus lateralis (NRL) and the nucleus recessus posterioris (NRP). The nuclei were found in the hypothalamus of numerous species, e.g., the gold fish, eel, and roach." [BTO:0003662, ISSN:1505-0297]
is_a: UBERON:0006568 {source="BTO"} ! hypothalamic nucleus

[Term]
id: UBERON:0036185
name: Sertoli cell barrier
def: "The blood-testis barrier (abbreviated as BTB) is a physical barrier between the blood vessels and the seminiferous tubules of the animal testes. The barrier is formed by tight connections between the Sertoli cells, which are sustentacular cells (supporting cells) of the seminiferous tubules, and nourish the spermatogonia. The barrier prevents passage of cytotoxic agents (bodies or substances that are toxic to cells) into the seminiferous tubules." [Wikipedia:Blood-testis_barrier]
synonym: "blood testis barrier" RELATED [Wikipedia:Blood-testis_barrier]
synonym: "blood-testes barrier" RELATED [Wikipedia:Blood-testis_barrier]
xref: MESH:D001814
xref: Wikipedia:Blood-testis_barrier
intersection_of: UBERON:0014914 ! haemolymphatic fluid-testis barrier
intersection_of: composed_primarily_of CL:0000216 ! Sertoli cell

