[Term]
id: UBERON:2001188
name: Weberian apparatus
def: "Anatomical cluster that consists of the anteriormost vertebrae and associated structures that connect the swim bladder to the inner ear." [ZFIN:curator]
comment: Vertebra 1-4, and sometimes vertebra 5 in some catfishes, are part of the Weberian apparatus. Weberian apparatus is present in Otophysi.
