[Term]
id: UBERON:6000046
name: insect dorsal appendage
def: "Paired appendage of the eggshell, located on the anterior-dorsal side of the egg, just posterior to the operculum. Functions as a respiratory structures." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172]
synonym: "chorionic appendage" EXACT [FlyBase:FBrf0047871]
is_a: UBERON:6007248 ! insect chorionic specialization

