creation_date: 2020-09-08T14:14:21Z

[Term]
id: UBERON:8400002
name: hepatic acinus zone 3
def: "The region of the hepatic acinus immediately surrounding the central veins. This region has the lowest oxygen concentration in the acinus. Zone 3 is located in the centrilobular region of the liver lobule, closest to the central vein. Hepatocytes in this region are the primary location for the biotransformation of drugs." [PMID:29763190]
