[Term]
id: UBERON:8480031
name: tooth root apical papilla
def: "The portion of the dental papilla located at the apex of the root of developing permanent tooth that is responsible for the progressive elongation and maturation of the root tooth." [PMID:18498881, PMID:34026757]
synonym: "apical papilla" EXACT [PMID:18215674]
synonym: "apical papilla of immature permanent teeth" EXACT [PMID:30834270]
is_a: UBERON:0000479 ! tissue
relationship: adjacent_to UBERON:0003677 ! tooth root
relationship: dc-contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473 ! Paula Duek Roggli
property_value: dcterms-date "2023-11-02T07:48:12Z" xsd:dateTime
property_value: editor_note "The surface layer is formed by a dense collagen matrix with perpendicular aligned collagen fibers. The inner layer consists of a loosely disorganized collagen matrix with a high concentration of mesenchymal stem cells. Fully mature roots lack apical papilla." xsd:string {xref="PMID:18498881", xref="PMID:34026757"}

