[Term]
id: UBERON:8600019
name: placental basal plate
def: "A maternal facing structure of the placental disc, adjacent to the intervillous space. Major components of the placental basal plate include decidua basalis, fibrinoid, connective tissue, extravillous trophoblasts, and residues of degenerating villi and maternal vessels." [PMID:17059842, PMID:32108320]
synonym: "PBP" RELATED OMO:0003000 [PMID:31002314]
synonym: "placenta basal plate" EXACT [PMID:32108320]
