[Term]
id: UBERON:8600050
name: trophoblast island
def: "An accumulation of extravillous trophoblast cells at the tip of a floating villus or occasionally attached to the chorionic plate embedded in fibrin." [doi:10.1007/978-3-030-84725-8]
comment: A trophoblast island is directly continuous with villous cytotrophoblast in places where the villous syncytiotrophoblast is interrupted. {xref="doi:10.1007/978-3-030-84725-8"}
