[Term]
id: UBERON:8600109
name: distal ureter
def: "A segment of the ureter that extends from the common iliac artery bifurcation to the bladder. From there, the ureter curves back and follows the lateral pelvic wall inferiorly to connect with the posterolateral bladder wall." [PMID:30422575]
synonym: "lower ureter" EXACT [PMID:30422575]
synonym: "pelvic ureter" EXACT [PMID:30422575]
