[Term]
id: UBERON:8600120
name: atrial intrinsic cardiac ganglion
def: "A ganglion that is part of the atrial region of the heart. The activation of efferent neurons in this ganglion results in the modulation of heart rate, atrio-ventricular node conduction, and inotropism of atria and ventricles." [ILX:0793555, PMID:23559611, PMID:33255284]
synonym: "atrial ganglionated plexus" RELATED [ILX:0793555]
xref: ILX:0793555
