[Term]
id: UBERON:8600129
name: corpus hemorrhagicum
def: "A transient, mesoderm-derived structure in the ovary that forms immediately after the rupture of a mature ovarian follicle during ovulation. It is formed by bleeding of small blood vessels in the follicle wall as the follicle collapses, resulting in a blood-filled center that rapidly clots. This structure develops into the corpus luteum." [https://ohiostate.pressbooks.pub/vethisto/chapter/13-the-ovary/, PMID:34330986, wikipedia:Corpus_hemorrhagicum]
synonym: "CH" RELATED OMO:0003000 [PMID:34330986]
